{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC segmenting MD→wiki renderer module (pure capability; codec untouched)\n\n## Context / Problem\nJira Data Center stores rich text as wiki markup (REST v2), a lossy text format.\nThe `RichTextCodec` seam (epic `e369`, story J3 / `aac8`) routes DC rich text\nthrough **`WikiTextCodec`** (`adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py:72`), today an\n**identity** codec: `fit_outbound` (`:82`), `normalize_outbound` (`:96`), `to_wire`\n(`:100`), `decode_inbound` (`:104`) all pass the plain string through. So DC ships\nrebar's raw Markdown as literal wiki source.\n\nNo library round-trips rebar's punctuation-dense prose: pandoc's jira reader\nmisparses `->`, ASCII pipe-tables, and regex, and provably erodes them one\ncharacter per pass (the ASCII-table body decays 9115→9110 monotonically). A\nwhole-body all-or-nothing conversion is echo-safe but only ~15% rich. A\n**segmenting** one-way renderer that converts only structurally-safe units and\npasses dangerous ones through verbatim reaches ~68% of bodies / ~78% of chars\nrich, proven non-corrupting across 23 environments, 6 authors, and an\nout-of-distribution corpus.\n\n**Why this story ships a pure module, not a codec change.** On DC — unlike Cloud —\nthe live outbound wire flows THROUGH a codec op: the shared\n`OutboundFieldMapper.map_fields_to_remote` composes the description as\n`normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(value))` at `outbound_mapper.py:77`, and that\nstring is what reaches `_issues.py:44 update_issue` → `issue.update(fields=…)`.\nThe codec law (ticket a32a) further ties `normalize_outbound(t)` to\n`decode_inbound(to_wire(t))` — parametrized over BOTH codecs at\n`test_rich_text_codec.py:163` — and the comment differ's dedup\n(`outbound_comments.py:48`) relies on it. Therefore **any change to\n`WikiTextCodec`'s `to_wire` or `normalize_outbound` is, on DC, an immediate live\ncutover** (a rendering `normalize_outbound` ships rendered wiki the instant it\nmerges) **and breaks the pinned identity tests**\n(`test_wiki_normalize_is_identity:251`,\n`test_wiki_codec_wire_shape_and_decode_are_the_plain_string:244`,\n`test_non_string_values_pass_through_untouched:183`) **and the codec law**. To\nkeep capability strictly separate from the hazardous cutover — which must land\ntogether with echo-safety in `3388` (which depends on this story) — **this story\ndelivers only the pure renderer module and its tests, and leaves `WikiTextCodec`\nfully identity.** Nothing observable changes on merge.\n\n## Prior art in this repo (the seam we build on — NOT greenfield)\n- `WikiTextCodec` (DC) — `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py:72`, identity today;\n  constructed into the shared `OutboundFieldMapper` at `backend.py:84`. **Left\n  unchanged by this story.**\n- `RichTextCodec` Protocol — four ops; the wire op is `to_wire` (DC: a wiki `str`).\n- **Codec law (ticket a32a):** `normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t))`\n  at `test_rich_text_codec.py:163`; today `WikiTextCodec` satisfies it trivially\n  (all ops identity). This story does not perturb it; `3388` re-establishes it for\n  the rendering codec when it wires the renderer in.\n- **Guard:** `backend.py:131 normalize_rich_text` is the **INBOUND** decode and\n  delegates to the SHARED plain-text `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` (ticket\n  21ca; also used by sibling repo `agentic-dev-platform`) — unchanged.\n- **Import contract (ADR 0035):** `jira_family/` must not import `adapters/jira/`.\n  pandoc/`pypandoc` is not a Cloud module, so the renderer lives in `jira_family/`.\n\n## Approach (pure renderer module)\nAdd `adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` exposing a pure function\n`render_markdown_to_wiki(md: str) -> str` (plus its internal segmenting helpers).\nIt is **not referenced by any codec op or live send path in this story** — it is\nunit/corpus-tested in isolation, ready for `3388` to wire into\n`WikiTextCodec.to_wire`.\n\nPipeline: split the body into blocks and list-items; render structurally-safe\nunits (headings, lists, code, quotes, safe paragraphs) to wiki via pinned\n`pandoc` (`-f commonmark -t jira --wrap=none`); pass dangerous units (ASCII\ntables, arrow/regex/HTML-dense prose) through **verbatim**; reassemble in original\norder. Two lossless render rules: **code-aware arrow substitution**\n(`-> <- <-> =>` → `→ ← ↔ ⇒`, prose-only, skipping fenced/inline code) which MUST\nrun on the **Markdown before pandoc**; and **verbatim-wrapping ASCII tables in\n`{noformat}`** to stop per-pass dash erosion.\n\n**pandoc delivery (portability).** Pin **`pypandoc-binary`** (bundles a pandoc\nbinary in the wheel) rather than bare `pypandoc` (which requires a system pandoc)\nso the DC path is self-contained in CI and prod. The renderer probes pandoc\navailability once; if pandoc is **absent or errors**, `render_markdown_to_wiki`\n**returns the input unchanged** (identity passthrough — echo-safe, never\ncorrupting) and logs once. GPL/SBOM compliance for the bundled binary is handled\nby the robustness story `5c0e`.\n\n## Corpus fixture (evaluability)\nThe ~68%/~78% coverage figures and the 179 code-arrow / 70 table-erosion\nregression counts are measured against a **vendored** fixture,\n`tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/` (a sanitized snapshot exported from the ticket\ncorpus, committed into the repo — NOT fetched from a live environment at test\ntime), so the tests are hermetic and the counts are reproducible in-session.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope for this story (owned by `3388`)\n- Wiring `render_markdown_to_wiki` into `WikiTextCodec.to_wire`, redefining\n  `normalize_outbound` to the compare form, and updating the DC identity pin tests\n  (`test_wiki_normalize_is_identity`, `test_wiki_codec_wire_shape_and_decode_are_the_plain_string`,\n  `test_non_string_values_pass_through_untouched`) + the codec-law test for the\n  rendering codec.\n- Applying the render on the live DC send (`outbound_mapper.py:77`) and CREATE\n  path (`backend.py:70`); the second-pass convergence proof; the rollback path.\nThis story leaves every codec op and live send site untouched, so no observable DC\nbehavior changes on merge.\n\n## Scope\n- `adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` (new) — segmenting renderer (split →\n  per-unit safe-render/passthrough → reassemble; arrow substitution; table wrap;\n  pandoc-availability probe + identity fallback). ADR-0035-clean. Pure module,\n  not wired to any codec.\n- `pyproject.toml` — pinned `pypandoc-binary` extra.\n- `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/` (new) — vendored, sanitized corpus fixture.\n- **Guard (UNCHANGED):** `WikiTextCodec` and all its ops\n  (`adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py`); `backend.py:131 normalize_rich_text`; the\n  live send sites `outbound_mapper.py:77` and `backend.py:70` (all wired by `3388`).\n- `tests/` — segmenting/arrow/table/coverage tests over the vendored fixture.\n\n## Testing (pure-module unit + fixture-corpus only)\n- Happy path: headings + a checklist + a fenced code block render to wiki\n  `h1.`/`*`-bullets/`{code}` via `render_markdown_to_wiki` and reassemble in order.\n- Danger passthrough: an ASCII pipe-table, a prose `->`, and a `obj->method()`\n  code arrow render with the table verbatim in `{noformat}`, prose `->`→`→`, and\n  the code arrow untouched.\n- pandoc-absent fallback: with pandoc unavailable, `render_markdown_to_wiki`\n  returns the input unchanged and logs once (`test_dc_pandoc_absent_identity`).\n- Codec untouched: `WikiTextCodec` stays identity — the existing\n  `test_wiki_normalize_is_identity`,\n  `test_wiki_codec_wire_shape_and_decode_are_the_plain_string`,\n  `test_non_string_values_pass_through_untouched`, and the codec-law test stay\n  green unmodified.\n- Corpus coverage/safety over `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/`: rich for ~68% of\n  bodies with 0 code-arrow rewrites and 0 prose corruptions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wiki_render.render_markdown_to_wiki` segments a body and renders only\n  structurally-safe units, passing dangerous units (tables/arrows/regex/HTML)\n  verbatim; verified by `test_dc_segmenting_passthrough` on a mixed body.\n- [ ] Code-aware arrow substitution runs on the Markdown before pandoc and touches\n  0 code arrows; verified by a test asserting `obj->method()` is unchanged while a\n  prose `->` becomes `→` (regression over the 179 known code-arrow bodies in\n  `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/`: 0 rewrites).\n- [ ] ASCII tables are verbatim-wrapped in `{noformat}` and do not erode across\n  passes; verified by `test_dc_table_noformat_stable` over the 70 known erosion\n  bodies in the fixture (70/70 stable).\n- [ ] `pypandoc-binary` is pinned and, when pandoc is unavailable,\n  `render_markdown_to_wiki` returns the input unchanged (echo-safe); verified by\n  `test_dc_pandoc_absent_identity`.\n- [ ] Over the vendored `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/` the renderer produces rich\n  output for ≈68% of bodies / ≈78% of chars with zero prose corruption; verified by\n  `test_dc_corpus_coverage`.\n- [ ] `WikiTextCodec` and all its ops remain identity and the live send sites are\n  unchanged by this story; verified by the existing DC codec identity tests\n  (`test_wiki_normalize_is_identity`,\n  `test_wiki_codec_wire_shape_and_decode_are_the_plain_string`,\n  `test_non_string_values_pass_through_untouched`) and the codec-law test staying\n  green unmodified (the observable cutover is `3388`)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785809660609689001,"uuid":"ee30748a-a2b5-44c9-8042-5fb8e5b26564"}